dure arms, exactly as declared.\",\n    \"The selected report demonstrates the issue: it feeds all 60 rows into a row-independent Welch two-sample t-test, explicitly stating 'Each harvest sample in the file supplies one observation, so the test runs on 30 observations per blend', and reports df = 57.9. Since each vessel's 5 rows are repeated measurements of the same culture, the true number of independent units is 6 per arm, not 30; the report treats within-vessel replicates as independent, inflating the effective sample size and degrees of freedom.\",\n    \"The [selected-result] conclusion ('chitin content is significantly higher on the starch blend', p < 0.001, 95% CI 0.67 to 2.33) rests on this pseudoreplicated n = 30 per arm; no vessel-level aggregation, mixed model, or clustered inference is performed anywhere in workflow/analysis.py, so the report demonstrates the issue rather than its absence.\",\n    \"No authority lock was minted (NO LOCK MINTED), so no lock's unit-key authorization exists to follow from the declaration; lock_follows_declaration is false.\"\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":6184,"ttft_stream_ms":1671,"time_to_request_ms":14,"type":"result","duration_ms":13716,"uuid":"22e43ac4-18d1-4257-b84e-76c780d0876f"}
